          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पगड़ी (pagṛī) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from paggā, \"headdress\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry (CDIAL 7644); the match is through Hindi pagṛī. CDIAL thinks a source in Sanskrit pragraha scarcely likely, and explains the ṛ as an added suffix."
            }
