          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लूगड़ो (lūgṛo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from lugga, \"defective\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL lists Old Marwari lovaṛī under it (CDIAL 11072). The Old Marwari row means \"a woman's waist garment\"; in the same large group of \"defective\" words, Hindi lugṛā means \"rag\" and Gujarati lugṛũ \"clothes\". How the senses connect is not settled."
            }
